## What I worked on

Today our team connected our separate parts into one shared project. We started combining the work from different branches and checked how the main project structure works together.

I also learned more about working with Git branches. With the help of my teammate Viktoria, I understood better how to create a separate branch, make changes, commit them, push the branch, and then merge the work into the main project. This helped me understand the team workflow more clearly.

In addition, I added a custom component called `PromoCountdownBanner`. This component is placed in the header and shows a promotional banner with a countdown timer for a store sale.

In this component, I used several Angular concepts:

- `@Component` decorator to define the component
- `@Input()` to receive data from the parent component, such as the banner title, button text, and sale end date
- `@Output()` to send events to the parent component when the user clicks the banner button or when the timer expires
- Interpolation `{{ }}` to display the title, button text, and countdown time
- Property binding to pass values from the parent component
- Event binding to handle user actions
- Lifecycle hooks such as `ngOnInit` and `ngOnDestroy` to start and clear the countdown timer

This component helped me practice component communication and understand how reusable Angular components can be used in a real online store project.

